    {
      "id": "p2",
      "number": 2,
      "title": "Problem 2",
      "sourcePages": [
        2,
        3
      ],
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "A bus company operates a number of routes connecting different bus stops in the city. Buses run in both directions along each route. The bus company hires a supervisor who has to periodically check that the signboards and waiting areas at each bus stop are in good condition."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "The supervisor needs to set up a central office at one of the bus stops. He would like to locate this office at a bus stop from where the maximum number of stops he has to travel to reach any other bus stop is minimized."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "For simplicity, the bus stops are identified by numbers rather than names. Bus routes are described by the sequence of bus stops that they pass through. Suppose, for example that we had the following set of bus stops and bus routes."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Bus stops 1,2,. . . ,6"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Route A 1—2—3"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Route B 2—4—7"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "Route C 2—4—5—6"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In this case the ideal location for the supervisor’s office is bus stop 4, because every other bus stop is at most two stops away. Notice that from bus stop 2, the supervisor can reach every other bus stop without changing buses, but bus stop 4 is better than bus stop 2 because from bus stop 2 it takes three stops to reach bus stop 6. The supervisor does not care about how many time he has to change buses; he only wants to minimize the maximum number of stops to every other bus stop."
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "text": "In the three problems below, you are given a set of bus stops and bus routes. Your task is to identify the ideal location for the supervisor’s central office in each case."
        }
      ],
      "parts": [
